@lang en
IMPORT `law36-vn28-fixtures`

-- Tests for Articles 34, 56-59, 62(5), 88 and 89, and Decision 1. Every expected value is read
-- from the line of the source cited beside it (src N = line N of the raw text), never from the
-- rules. Thresholds are tested on both sides. The two generated blocks (ages, terms) were
-- written by a script from the source lines they cite.

§ `Tests — vehicles, licences, drivers`

§§ `Article 34 — the kinds (src 252-302)`

-- (g) moped: two wheels, design speed not above 50 km/h, heat engine not above 50 cm3 (src 278-283).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a petrol vehicle on` 2 `wheels, of` 50 `cm3, designed for` 50 `km/h, kerb mass` 90) EQUALS `a moped`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a petrol vehicle on` 2 `wheels, of` 51 `cm3, designed for` 50 `km/h, kerb mass` 90) EQUALS `a motorcycle`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a petrol vehicle on` 2 `wheels, of` 50 `cm3, designed for` 51 `km/h, kerb mass` 90) EQUALS `a motorcycle`
-- (g): electric motor not above 4 kW (src 283-284).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`an electric vehicle on` 2 `wheels, of` 4 `kW, designed for` 50 `km/h, kerb mass` 90) EQUALS `a moped`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`an electric vehicle on` 2 `wheels, of` 4.1 `kW, designed for` 50 `km/h, kerb mass` 90) EQUALS `a motorcycle`
-- (e) a three-wheeled motorcycle has a kerb mass not above 400 kg; (a) a three-wheeler above 400 kg is an automobile (src 256-257, 275-277).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a petrol vehicle on` 3 `wheels, of` 110 `cm3, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 400) EQUALS `a motorcycle`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a petrol vehicle on` 3 `wheels, of` 110 `cm3, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 401) EQUALS `an automobile`
-- (d) four-wheeled motorised passenger vehicle: at most 30 km/h and 15 persons besides the driver (src 265-268).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying persons` `with` 15 `seats, designed for` 30 `km/h, kerb mass` 900 `, one chassis` FALSE `, rows of seats` 4 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 10)) EQUALS `a four-wheeled motorised passenger vehicle`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying persons` `with` 15 `seats, designed for` 31 `km/h, kerb mass` 900 `, one chassis` FALSE `, rows of seats` 4 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 10)) EQUALS `an automobile`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying persons` `with` 16 `seats, designed for` 30 `km/h, kerb mass` 900 `, one chassis` FALSE `, rows of seats` 4 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 10)) EQUALS `an automobile`
-- (đ) four-wheeled motorised goods vehicle: one chassis, at most two rows and 5 persons, 60 km/h, 550 kg kerb, an electric motor at most 15 kW (src 269-274).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 5 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 2 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 15)) EQUALS `a four-wheeled motorised goods vehicle`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 5 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 551 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 2 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 15)) EQUALS `an automobile`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 5 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 2 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 16)) EQUALS `an automobile`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 6 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 2 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 15)) EQUALS `an automobile`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 5 `seats, designed for` 61 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 2 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 15)) EQUALS `an automobile`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 5 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` FALSE `, rows of seats` 2 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 15)) EQUALS `an automobile`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 5 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 3 `, motor` (`an electric motor` 15)) EQUALS `an automobile`
-- (đ) caps only an electric motor; a heat-engine four-wheeler of 60 km/h and 550 kg is still (đ) (src 273-274).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a four-wheeler for` `carrying goods` `with` 2 `seats, designed for` 60 `km/h, kerb mass` 550 `, one chassis` TRUE `, rows of seats` 1 `, motor` (`a heat engine` 800)) EQUALS `a four-wheeled motorised goods vehicle`
-- (b), (c): a trailer, and a semi-trailer resting partly on its tractor (src 259-264); (3)(d): one towed by a tractor is a special-use machine (src 299).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a towed vehicle of` 3000 `kg gross, resting partly on the towing vehicle` FALSE `, special-use kind` NOTHING) EQUALS `a trailer`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a towed vehicle of` 30000 `kg gross, resting partly on the towing vehicle` TRUE `, special-use kind` NOTHING) EQUALS `a semi-trailer`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a towed vehicle of` 3000 `kg gross, resting partly on the towing vehicle` FALSE `, special-use kind` (JUST `a trailer or semi-trailer towed by a tractor`)) EQUALS `a special-use machine`
-- (3)(c): a tractor is a special-use machine, not a motor vehicle (src 298).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a tractor with payload in kg` 1000) EQUALS `a special-use machine`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 34(1) — a motor vehicle` (`a tractor with payload in kg` 1000)
#ASSERT `Article 34(1) — a motor vehicle` (`a petrol vehicle on` 2 `wheels, of` 50 `cm3, designed for` 50 `km/h, kerb mass` 90)
-- (2)(a)-(b): a bicycle, and a motor-assisted bicycle, are rudimentary (src 287-290); (g) excludes the latter from the mopeds (src 284).
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a bicycle moved by` `a motor that only assists pedalling, cut off when the rider stops pedalling or at 25 km/h`) EQUALS `a motor-assisted bicycle`
#ASSERT `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a bicycle moved by` `human power, through pedals or a hand crank`) EQUALS `another rudimentary vehicle`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 34(1) — a motor vehicle` (`a bicycle moved by` `a motor that only assists pedalling, cut off when the rider stops pedalling or at 25 km/h`)
-- A one-wheeled motor vehicle answers no limb: declined by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 34 — the kind of` (`a petrol vehicle on` 1 `wheels, of` 50 `cm3, designed for` 30 `km/h, kerb mass` 40) BECAUSE "the vehicle answers no limb of Article 34, and whether it is a similar vehicle under Article 34(1)(h) or (2)(e) is not decided in this model"

